  <!-- PROPERTY TYPES -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">HUYTON HOMES WE COVER</span>
      <h2>One Plumber. Every Type of L36 Home.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Huyton has a real mix of housing. Old council semis, private estates, new builds and some Victorian streets. Here's what we usually find.</p>
      <div class="pf-why-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">

        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>1950s and 1960s Council Semis</h3>
          <p>The bulk of Huyton stock. Three-bed family layouts. Most were bought through right-to-buy from the 1980s on. Each one was upgraded piecemeal. Mixed pipe materials, mixed boiler ages. We diagnose what's there before quoting any work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>1980s and 1990s Private Estates</h3>
          <p>Streets off Knowsley Lane, Whiston Lane and the newer developments. Copper pipework with compression fittings, now 30 to 40 years old. The joints harden and start to weep. Same-visit fix in most cases.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Court Hey and Roby Detached</h3>
          <p>The more affluent Huyton pockets. Larger detached and semi-detached family homes. Often two bathrooms, sometimes unvented cylinders. We're G3 qualified for that work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Modern New Builds on Knowsley Lane</h3>
          <p>The newer estates by Your Housing Group and other developers. Modern combi boilers, push-fit plumbing, often still under maker warranty. We honour warranty terms when we work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Stockbridge Village and Page Moss</h3>
          <p>The bigger estate areas. Mix of original 1960s stock and 1990s refurbs. Strong landlord and rental presence. We cover landlord call-outs and do CP12 paperwork for L36 portfolios.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Victorian Terraces Near the Station</h3>
          <p>The older streets close to Huyton railway station. Lead supply pipes, cast iron waste, 130 years of part-upgrades. We work on them every week.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


