  <!-- LOCAL KNOWLEDGE SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">HUYTON LOCAL KNOWLEDGE</span>
      <h2>What L36 Plumbing Really Looks Like</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Huyton is in Knowsley Borough Council, not Liverpool City Council. Page Moss ward, St Michaels ward, St Gabriels ward. All Knowsley. Same as Kirkby where we're based.</p>

        <p>The bulk of Huyton housing went up in the 1950s and 1960s. Council semis built for families on three-bed family layouts. Solid brick, decent gardens, big enough to be a forever home. Most were sold to tenants through right-to-buy from the 1980s on. Each home was then upgraded at a different time. That's why no two homes have the same plumbing today.</p>

        <p>That patchwork is the L36 reality. Lead pipe meets copper meets plastic in unexpected places. A 1970s boiler in one home, a 2022 combi in the next. We work it all out before we quote.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>Huyton-with-Roby is the heart of L36. The Liverpool to Manchester railway line runs straight through, with Huyton station and Roby station both busy. The Tesco Extra is a local landmark. Court Hey Park sits to the south.</p>

        <p>Beyond the original council estate, the newer pockets are different again. Court Hey and parts of Roby have larger detached family homes. The Knowsley Lane new builds are post-2010 with modern boilers and push-fit plumbing. Stockbridge Village to the north is a separate estate that's been through its own redevelopment.</p>

        <p>We work all of it. Same fixed rates either side of any boundary.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COMMON JOBS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Common Emergency Jobs in Huyton</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">What we attend most often in L36.</p>
      <div class="jobs-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">

        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>1950s Copper Pipe Pinhole Leaks</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">15 min response</span></div>
          <p>Original copper pipework in 1950s Huyton semis is now 70 years old. It develops pinhole leaks in the loft, under floors and behind kitchen units. We patch the failing section. Where multiple pinholes show up, we recommend a repipe.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Old Boiler Replacement</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">15 min response</span></div>
          <p>A boiler over 20 years old with regular faults is almost always cheaper to replace than repair. We fit Worcester Bosch, Vaillant and Ideal from £1,800. 10-year warranty. ECO4 grant check included on every quote.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Compression Joint Weeping</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">15 min response</span></div>
          <p>1980s and 1990s Huyton estates have compression joints now 30 to 40 years old. The olive inside hardens. The seal starts to weep. We cut out the old fitting and put in a new one. Under an hour in most cases.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Right-to-Buy Mixed Pipework Faults</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">15 min response</span></div>
          <p>Right-to-buy homes have been upgraded piecemeal over decades. Lead, copper and plastic all meet at random joints. The joins fail. We figure out what's there and fix the failed section the right way.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Blocked Drains</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">15 min response</span></div>
          <p>The older clay drain runs are 70 years old. Roots find their way in. Lead joints fail. Ground movement cracks pipes. We clear with high-pressure jetting. CCTV survey on request.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Landlord Emergencies</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">15 min response</span></div>
          <p>Huyton has a strong rental market. We cover landlord call-outs 24/7. Photos, fault reports and itemised invoices for insurance claims. CP12 paperwork for portfolios at batch rates.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- WHAT TO DO SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>While You Wait For Our Engineer</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Four steps to protect your home while we're on the way.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">1</span><div><strong>Find the stopcock and turn it off</strong><p>For any water leak, the stopcock is your first move. In most Huyton semis it's under the kitchen sink or near the front door. In newer estates it's often in the airing cupboard. Turn it clockwise to stop all water.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, get out</strong><p>Don't touch any switches. Open windows as you leave. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--orange);font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then us on 0151 558 0334 once the home is safe.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>No heating? Check the pressure gauge</strong><p>Look at the gauge on the boiler. It should sit between 1 and 1.5 bar. Below 0.5, you can top it up with the filling loop underneath. That fixes about half of all "no heating" calls. If it doesn't, call us.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph the damage</strong><p>Take photos and video before you start cleaning. Insurance claims need proof. We give you our own fault report with photos as well, ready for your insurer or landlord.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


